  "paper": "paper_2",
  "question": {
    "html": "<section class=\"context\"><p>A fixed mass of an ideal gas is taken through a cycle that consists of three processes:</p>\n<table><tbody><tr><td></td><td><p>X → Y</p></td><td><p>Isothermal compression from a pressure of 0.10 MPa and volume of 1.20 × 10<sup>−3 </sup>m<sup>3</sup> to a pressure of 0.48 MPa</p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td><p>Y → Z</p></td><td><p>Isobaric expansion</p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td><p>Z → X</p></td><td><p>Adiabatic expansion to the initial state</p></td></tr></tbody></table></section><section class=\"question-part\" data-label=\"a\"><p><strong>a</strong> </p><p>Draw, on the axes, the pV diagram for this cycle. X and Y are plotted for you. Numbers are not required on the axes.</p>\n<p><figure data-asset-id=\"fig_01\"><img alt=\"Source question diagram 1\" src=\"asset:fig_01\"/></figure></p><p>[2]</p></section><section class=\"question-part\" data-label=\"b\"><p><strong>b</strong> Show that the volume of the gas at Y is 0.25 × 10<sup>−3 </sup>m<sup>3</sup>. [1]</p></section><section class=\"question-part\" data-label=\"c\"><p><strong>c</strong> </p><p>An algebraic statement of the first law of thermodynamics is Q = ΔU + W.</p>\n<p>Data for the cycle are provided in the table.</p>\n<p><figure data-asset-id=\"fig_02\"><img alt=\"Source question diagram 2\" src=\"asset:fig_02\"/></figure></p><p></p></section><section class=\"question-part\" data-label=\"c.i\"><p><strong>c.i</strong> Annotate the table with the missing values. Use the answer box below for your calculations. [3]</p></section><section class=\"question-part\" data-label=\"c.ii\"><p><strong>c.ii</strong> Determine the volume of the gas at Z. [2]</p></section><section class=\"question-part\" data-label=\"c.iii\"><p><strong>c.iii</strong> Determine the efficiency of this cycle. [2]</p></section><section class=\"question-part\" data-label=\"d\"><p><strong>d</strong> Outline why this theoretical cycle is unsuitable for use in a practical heat engine. [2]</p></section>"
  },
